## Summary

The bug was in the chat widget's message submission logic at `codex-rs/tui/src/chatwidget.rs:6413`.

When building the user turn operation, the code explicitly set `permission_profile` to `None` whenever the sandbox policy was the `SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox { .. }` variant:

```rust
let permission_profile = if matches!(
    self.config.permissions.sandbox_policy.get(),
    SandboxPolicy::ExternalSandbox { .. }
) {
    None
} else {
    Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile())
};
```

This dropped the session's configured permission profile precisely for the external sandbox case. I replaced it so the profile is always preserved, regardless of sandbox policy variant:

```rust
let permission_profile = Some(self.config.permissions.permission_profile());
```

The `SandboxPolicy` import remains used elsewhere in the file, and `cargo check -p codex-tui` passes. No test files were touched.
